Grey out inactive #if regions: LSP-only Unnecessary/Hint diagnostics for preprocessor-dead code

Requested 2026-08-29 by Max, follow-up to B030: can an IDE grey out code that
is dead because of the current defines, using the same Unnecessary tag?

## Approach
`DiagnosticTag::UNNECESSARY` on a HINT-severity diagnostic spanning each
inactive region. VS Code fades the range (`editor.showUnused`) and HINT keeps
it out of the Problems panel. This is what clangd does for `#if 0` blocks.
The non-portable alternatives (clangd's custom
`textDocument/inactiveRegions` notification, a bespoke semantic-token
modifier) only work in one client each — not worth it. B030 already ships the
tag plumbing.

## Gap
`preprocess()` (src/preprocessor/filter.rs:75) masks inactive lines with
spaces, preserving byte offsets exactly, but `PreprocessResult`
(src/preprocessor/filter.rs:29) carries only `masked_source` + `errors` — the
per-line mask decision is discarded. The filter must also emit the regions.

## Design calls (agreed with Max)
1. LSP-only, NOT `check`. A plugin with hundreds of `#if MP4` lines would
   spew hints into CLI output and the TUI, and HINT does not save us there —
   `check` prints hints. Call the new emitter only from the two server
   sites in src/server/mod.rs (sharded + non-sharded), never from
   `run_check` in src/cli/mod.rs.
2. Body only, not the directive lines. `#if` / `#else` / `#endif` stay at
   normal weight; only the dead body is faded. Matches clangd and keeps the
   structure readable.
3. One diagnostic per coalesced region, outermost only. A nested `#if`
   inside an already-dead block must not stack a second overlapping range.

## Plan
- `PreprocessResult` gains `inactive_regions: Vec<Span>` — contiguous dead
  bodies, outermost only, directive lines excluded.
- New `InactiveLevel { Ignore, Hint, Info }` config enum, default `Hint`,
  resolved through the same ladder as `unused` (TOML key, user config,
  initializationOptions, and a CLI flag only insofar as it is a config key).
  Deliberately no warn/error: a dead branch is dead by design, not a defect,
  and `error` would let one key fail `check` on every `#if MP4`.
- Emitter builds one HINT/INFO diagnostic per region, tagged UNNECESSARY,
  code `inactive-region`, message naming the condition that is off.
- VS Code extension: `openplanetLsp.inactiveRegions` enum, unset default,
  same "only forward what the user set" contract as B030.

## Test plan (TDD, red first)
Preprocessor (pure, no LSP):
- simple `#if OFF` body → one region covering the body only; the `#if` and
  `#endif` lines are NOT in it.
- `#if ON / #else / #endif` → the else body is the region; and the mirror
  case `#if OFF` → the if body is the region, else body is not.
- `#elif` chains: exactly the non-taken arms are regions; the taken arm is
  never a region (including when the taken arm is an `#elif`).
- nested `#if OFF { #if ON ... }` → ONE outermost region, not two.
- nested `#if ON { #if OFF ... }` → the inner body only.
- adjacent dead blocks separated by a live line → two regions, not coalesced.
- adjacent dead lines inside one block → one region, not per-line.
- unterminated `#if` at EOF → region runs to EOF, no panic.
- empty dead body (`#if OFF` immediately followed by `#endif`) → no
  zero-width region emitted.
- byte offsets round-trip: every region span slices out of the ORIGINAL
  source (not the masked one) and every byte inside it is masked in
  `masked_source` (guards offset drift).
- CRLF and multi-byte content inside a dead body → spans stay on char
  boundaries.

Server:
- level map: Ignore → no diagnostics, Hint → HINT, Info → INFORMATION.
- every emitted diagnostic carries `DiagnosticTag::UNNECESSARY` and code
  `inactive-region`, at both levels.
- generalise over what is dead: a function body, a whole function, a class
  member, a global, and an `#if` inside a namespace.
- CLI guard (the point of design call 1): `check` output on a fixture with a
  dead `#if` must contain NO inactive-region diagnostic at any level, and
  exit 0.
- ladder: TOML key / user config / initializationOptions each resolve it,
  workspace beats user, init options beat both (mirrors the B030 tests).

Extension (vitest): unset/empty/whitespace forwards nothing; each valid level
forwards verbatim; invalid dropped.